result={'status':'TWO ANKLE ROUTES NEUTRAL STATIC CLEAR; PRECONNECTED HOUSING DELTA CLEAR','wholeHarnessAccepted':False,'physicalFitVerified':False,'units':'mm','coordinateTransform':'identity','parts':parts,'routes':routes,'replaceRouteIds':['ttl-02-01','ttl-07-06'],'activeTopology':str(M/'active-topology.json'),'sourceHashes':{str(D/n):sha(D/n)for n in files}|{str(M/'active-topology.json'):sha(M/'active-topology.json')},'acceptance':{'referencePartPairs':f['expectedPairs'],'referenceCoverageComplete':f['complete'],'unexpectedWireOrExternalHousingIntersections':0,'interStrandPairs':len(r['wireWire']),'selfPrimitivePairs':len(s['rows']),'rawAllBoxesZeroIntersection':False,'ownMatingEnvelopeContacts':hits,'ownMatingInterpretation':'These four contacts are confined to the selected own motor case profile beside the selected EHR/B3B interface. ROBOTIS specifies EHR-3-compatible mating. The full rectangular catalogue envelope fills spaces absent from the real shaped housing. Preserve the measured negative: detailed plastic mating and latch geometry are not certified. This classification does not waive any wire, printed obstacle, other motor, or insertion travel.'},'assembly':[{'operation':'leg-01','prepare':'With power disconnected, identify motor IDs 2/7 and the registered socket. Preinsert this cable end before seating the knee motor into the orange thigh. Keep the cable free, not trapped under the motor or reinforcing plate.','check':'Full plug receiving body carried with knee motor along mirrored 45 mm guide approaches is clear against thigh and neighbouring motor bounds at 0.25 mm samples.'},{'operation':'leg-05','prepare':'Preinsert the other cable end in motor IDs 1/6 before putting that motor into the loose ankle fork. Feed the free soft length through the open side; keep the lower link and retaining screws off.','check':'Added plug body carried with motor from +Z30 into ankle/sleeve is sampled clear at 0.25 mm. This does not erase the existing bare-motor/fork source-contact fit boundary.'},{'operation':'leg-07/08/09','prepare':'Arrange the source exit towards the central thigh opening, then turn inboard before descending past the lip. Arrange the ankle return beside the lower-link end. Keep the 180 mm surplus as an accessible soft loop while joining the lower module; close retention only after checking both wire exits.','check':'Observe all three conductors clear of the lower rod, thigh lip, fastener seats and linkage. Do not pull tight or force the visual loop into an exact rigid shape.'},{'operation':'existing assembled legs','prepare':'The ordinary 15 mm straight insertion path is blocked by thigh at the knee and ankle/lower link at the ankle. Do not push a plug through those solids or remove the unrelated black reinforcing plate as a presumed remedy. If not prewired, reopen only the corresponding original motor/fork retention to return to the above preconnection stages; no new printed part is required.','check':'This report does not certify a shorter tilted recovery insertion or unchanged fully assembled access.'}],'remainingScope':['Physical plug/latch seating and hand access; the receiving housing is catalogue outline, not detailed female latch CAD.','Flexible joint motion, snag risk and actual slack dressing with the assembled robot; no rigid sweep of the whole neutral soft loop is prescribed.','Existing original ankle bare-motor/fork and lower-link physical fitting boundaries remain in the mechanical guide; cable delta checks do not supersede them.','Strand slot/colour is geometric only; confirm manufacturer keyed electrical pin assignment before applying power.'],'primarySources':[{'url':'https://www.jst-mfg.com/product/pdf/eng/eEH.pdf','local':str(D/'sources/jst-eh.pdf'),'use':'EHR-3 profile, 2.5 mm pitch and compatible conductor insulation range; not a manufacturer bend-radius claim.'},{'url':'https://emanual.robotis.com/docs/en/dxl/x/xl330-m288/','use':'Official XL330 TTL connector compatibility; source native male headers are separately registered to motor local geometry.'}]}
